   "slot": "member1_opening",
   "text": "A price crash fits LUSD's liquidation mechanism because the Stability Pool absorbs debt from troves that fall below their maintenance collateral ratio, and any remaining shortfall is redistributed pro rata to surviving troves rather than sold. In this scenario, no forced sales occur against exit liquidity because the absorption path eliminates the need for a sell-side bound.\n\nCollateral coverage remains at 3.71 before and after the shock, with zero bad debt reported. The system collateral ratio stays at 3.71, well above the Recovery Mode threshold, so no recovery mode is triggered.\n\nThe Stability Pool balance available to absorb liquidations in this scenario is $7.6M, which is the balance less the scenario's liquidity-provider flight share. Liquidity providers leave a share of zero in this scenario, and the exit liquidity remains at $8.3M.",
