   "slot": "member2_opening",
   "text": "A depeg of the paired stablecoin fits this token's mechanism because it is structurally insulated; exposure arises only through recomputed exit-liquidity curves. In the Member-2 headline scenario, forced sales are $0 and the ratio of forced sales to exit liquidity is 0.\n\nWhen the paired stablecoin trades at 0.88, exit liquidity totals $6.1M at a 0.5% price impact, rising to $7.8M at a 5.0% price impact. At 0.93, liquidity is $6.5M at 0.5% and $8.2M at 5.0%. At 0.97, liquidity reaches $6.8M at 0.5% and $8.6M at 5.0%.\n\nThese figures show that while the token avoids forced sales by construction, its resilience depends on the depth of these exit venues under stress.",
