   "slot": "counterfactual_explanations",
   "text": "The counterfactual scenario shows the price feed falling back from Chainlink to the Tellor oracle, which changes how the system observes market prices. This shift means the metric affected is none, indicating that no computed value exists for this specific fallback line because it records only the feed's constants and scope rather than a calculated result. The reader should take from this difference that the mechanism relies on instant observation of the PriceFeed at run_block without an EMA lag, as Liquity v1 lacks both LLAMMA and per-market price EMAs. Consequently, the price basis remains the bundle's own external collateral value divided by the external collateral sum, not a re-simulated fetchPrice call.",
