   "slot": "admin_surface_narrative",
   "text": "The system states that no admin power can alter backing — immutable. Every function, including minting, setting ceilings, upgrading code, pausing operations, freezing assets, blacklisting addresses, setting oracles, changing parameters, and seizing funds, is marked as immutable with a delay of 0 seconds and no veto address.\n\nEach capability has an owner that reads contract data but cannot change the underlying rules. The absence_read status applies to minting ceilings, upgrades, pauses, asset freezes, blacklists, oracle settings, parameter changes, and seizures for specific owners, while contract_read applies to others. No holder type exists beyond none, and no bucket or delay modifies the immediate effect of any action.\n\nBecause all admin functions are immutable and execute instantly without veto, the backing cannot be changed by any entity listed in the rows. The only way to alter these conditions would be a change to the contract itself, which is also marked as immutable.",
   "think": false,
   "total_duration": 652762251600,
